==Fundraising==
Under New Zealand electoral law, registered political parties are required to report any individual donations above $20,000 to the [[Electoral Commission (New Zealand)|Electoral Commission]] within 20 days during an election year. During a non-election year, political parties are required to report all donations above $6,000, most anonymous donations over $1,000 (except those protected from disclosure), any overseas donations over $50 and the quantity and total sum of any large donations that were not made anonymously in their annual returns.<ref name="Neville 14 Apr 2026">{{cite web |last1=Neville |first1=Alice |title=Who's funding who in election year? |url=https://thespinoff.co.nz/politics/14-04-2026/whos-funding-who-in-election-year |website=[[The Spinoff]] |access-date=16 April 2026 |date=14 April 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260416023840/https://thespinoff.co.nz/politics/14-04-2026/whos-funding-who-in-election-year |archive-date=16 April 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> By 24 October 2026, the following parties had received the following amounts in electoral donations; with the table's figures  below also including electoral donations from the 2025 calendar year.<ref name="Hancock 24 Sep 2026">{{cite news |last1=Hancock |first1=Farah |title=Political donations tracker: ACT gets another $225,000 and overall parties total exceeds 2023 campaign |url=https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/politics/647946/political-donations-tracker-act-gets-another-dollar225-000-and-overall-parties-total-exceeds-2023-campaign |access-date=4 October 2026 |work=[[RNZ]] |date=24 September 2026}}</ref><ref name="RNZ donations 7 May 2026">{{cite news |last1=Dexter |first1=Giles |title=National tops party donations list, ACT overtakes Labour |url=https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/political/594551/national-tops-party-donations-list-act-overtakes-labour |access-date=18 May 2026 |work=[[Radio New Zealand]] |date=7 May 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260507230814/https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/political/594551/national-tops-party-donations-list-act-overtakes-labour |archive-date=7 May 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>
