===Third party promoters and others===
Third party promoters, such as [[trade union]]s and [[lobby group]]s, can campaign during the three-month regulated period before election day. Promoters are required to register with the [[Electoral Commission (New Zealand)|Electoral Commission]] if they intend to spend over NZ$17,000 on campaigning during that period. Registered promoters spending over NZ$100,000 are required to report their expenses to the Electoral Commission.<ref name="2026 third party promoters">{{cite web |title=Register of promoters for the 2026 General a election |url=https://elections.nz/guidance-and-rules/for-third-party-promoters/register-of-promoters-for-the-2026-general-election |publisher=[[Electoral Commission (New Zealand)|Electoral Commission]] |access-date=21 October 2026}}</ref>

