== Voting ==
[[File:Voting sign Wellington railway station 2026.jpg|thumb|Sign at [[Wellington railway station]], pointing towards a voting place]]
Enrolments closed on 26 October, with advance voting beginning on the same day. By 24 October, 92.4 percent of eligible voters had registered to vote. During the 2023 general election, 94.7 percent of eligible voters had enrolled by election day; which was previously the closing date for enrolment.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Crimp |first1=Lauren |title=Enrolments closed, advance voting begins for 2026 Election |url=https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/politics_election-2026/2159477/enrolments-closed-advance-voting-begins-for-2026-election |access-date=29 October 2026 |work=[[RNZ]] |date=26 October 2026}}</ref> On 29 October, the Electoral Commission referred two people to police after claims they had voted multiple times. Under Section 215 of the Electoral Act 1993, it is an offence to vote more than once.<ref>{{cite news |title=Two people referred to police after allegedly voting 'multiple times' |url=https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/crime-and-justice/2215569/two-people-referred-to-police-after-allegedly-voting-multiple-times |access-date=29 October 2026 |work=[[RNZ]] |date=29 October 2026}}</ref>

== Results ==
A preliminary count of ordinary votes will take place on election day, 7 November. Ordinary votes cast in advance may be counted from 9:00&nbsp;am under secure conditions, while ordinary votes cast on election day will be counted after polling places close at 7:00&nbsp;pm. Preliminary results will be released progressively from 7:00&nbsp;pm as polling places report their counts. The Electoral Commission aims to have 50% of polling places reporting by 10:00&nbsp;pm and 95% by 11:30&nbsp;pm. [[Special vote]]s are not counted on election night.<ref name="Website-2">{{Cite web |title=How are general election votes counted? |url=https://elections.nz/democracy-in-nz/about-elections/how-are-general-election-votes-counted |access-date=2026-10-13 |website=elections.nz}}</ref>

Following election night, voting papers and electoral rolls will be returned to their respective electorate returning officers, a process that can take up to ten days for special votes. A master electoral roll will be compiled to identify any instances of multiple voting, and special votes will be processed and checked. All votes will then undergo an official count. The Electoral Commission is scheduled to declare the official results on 27 November 2026, 20 days after the election.<ref name="Website-1" /><ref name="Website-2" />

